	(text "THE GRAPHICS RAM: ADDRESS MULTIPLEXERS, WRITE BUFFER, THE TWO READ PATHS, BYTE LATCH, SHIFTER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e0452ca0-2559-5c7a-94b8-9b94f00e775d"))
	(text "IC24-IC27 give the RAM the display's address (DPAGE, RA3-0, SA9-0, D3) or the CPU's (CPAGE, PLANE3-0,\nADDR10-0): SELCPU. IC32 takes the display's byte on D2's rise and IC33 loads it with the text's (TLOAD).\nIC29 puts the bus on the RAM's data lines while -WE is low. A window read: in slot mode from IC30, which takes\nthe RAM's byte as each CPU slot ends (RDCK); in direct mode through IC31. These parts are the text-only\nbuild's left-off ones (with IC34, sheet 6)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0025bacc-e302-539c-9947-6d87dba070cf"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
